Fig. 4 of the paper (tt̄ vs HH(170) at parton level after the trigger, cross-fitted f_tt̄ of study_cv):

  1. write the inputs (theta, phi, y), from the repository root:
     mkdir -p results/plotting/paper/fig4_HH170 && .venv/bin/python - <<'PY'
     import numpy as np
     z = np.load("results/analysis/study_cv/scores_parton_trig.npz")
     for cache, ys, name in (("tt_fit", z["tt_cv"], "tt_f_theta_phi.txt"), ("HH170_all", z["HH170_cv"], "HH170_f_theta_phi.txt")):
         c = np.load(f"results/analysis/study_gonogo/cache/{cache}.npz")
         th, ph = np.arccos(np.clip(c["parton_trig/cos_theta"], -1, 1)), c["parton_trig/phi"]
         np.savetxt(f"results/plotting/paper/fig4_HH170/{name}", np.column_stack([th, ph, ys]), fmt="%.7g", header="theta phi y")
     PY
  2. cd results/plotting/paper/fig4_HH170 && ../../../.venv/bin/python ../../../code/plotting/paper/fig4_HH170/compare_y_fig4.py tt_f_theta_phi.txt HH170_f_theta_phi.txt t
     -> results/plotting/paper/fig4_HH170/tt_f_theta_phi_t.pdf (= fig4_dNdy_ttbar_HH170.pdf in the paper)

compare_y_fig4.py is a configured copy of ../compare_y.py (HH_170 labels, projection ratios on, y rescaled).
It writes its figures to results/plotting/paper/fig4_HH170/ wherever it is run from; the .txt inputs are read as given.
The .txt inputs are not kept in git.
